---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Rawan Aladdin — For Abaka AI"
  description="A targeted mini-portfolio: a design system built from scratch, a dense product interface, and shipped AI product work by Rawan Aladdin, for the Abaka AI Product Designer role."
  bodyClass="ab-pitch"
  canonical="https://rawanaladdin.com/abaka"
  noindex
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/abaka.css" />
  </Fragment>

  <main>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ HERO ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="hero" class="ab-section" style="min-height: 100vh; justify-content: flex-end; padding-bottom: 8rem;">
      <p class="ab-hero-label">For Abaka AI — October 2026</p>
      <h1 class="ab-hero-h1">Hi Abaka,<br>I'm Rawan.</h1>
      <p class="ab-hero-sub">
        A product designer who builds the system first and stays with it through build.
        Your posting asks for a design system from scratch, a dense tool that stays clear,
        and someone who works closely with engineers. This page is the evidence for each.
      </p>
      <div class="ab-hero-links">
        <a href="mailto:hello@rawanaladdin.com" class="main-link">hello@rawanaladdin.com &#8599;</a>
        <a href="/projects.html" class="main-link">full portfolio &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="ab-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ WHY ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="why" class="ab-section">
      <p class="ab-section-label">Why me, for this role</p>
      <h2 class="ab-h2">Three things<br>I'd bring.</h2>

      <div class="ab-ladder">

        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">01</p>
          <h3>I've built a design system from nothing.</h3>
          <p>
            For feeds I wrote the foundations myself: a palette with usage ratios and an AA
            contrast floor, a five-step type scale, fifteen icons on one grid, and logo rules,
            documented across eleven pages. Then I put it into the product.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">02</p>
          <h3>I've designed for a dense, data-heavy tool.</h3>
          <p>
            feeds is a reader for security analysts. Every article carries extracted
            vulnerability, malware and indicator tags inline, and saved filters gather them
            into a Smart Inbox. The interface has to stay calm with all of that on screen.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">03</p>
          <h3>I know what happens between the file and the shipped screen.</h3>
          <p>
            I applied feeds into the engineer's codebase through his code review, and I was
            the lead developer on Onward, an AI product. So handoff and quality review are
            familiar ground from both sides of the table.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="ab-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════ PROJECT 01 — FEEDS ═══════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="feeds" class="ab-section">
      <p class="ab-section-label">Project 01 — A design system, from scratch to production</p>
      <div class="ab-project-head">
        <h2 class="ab-project-title">feeds</h2>
        <span class="ab-meta">Designer · Brand system &amp; product UI · 2026</span>
      </div>
      <p class="ab-lede">
        A self-hosted, local-first reader and digest engine for security analysts, built by
        a developer client. The engine is his; everything you can see is mine.
      </p>

      <div class="ab-tags">
        <span class="ab-tag">Design System</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Foundations</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Iconography</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Product UI</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Accessibility</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Engineering Handoff</span>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-spec">
        <div>
          <div class="ab-spec-n">11</div>
          <div class="ab-spec-l">Pages of<br>guidelines</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ab-spec-n">5</div>
          <div class="ab-spec-l">Colours, with<br>usage ratios</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ab-spec-n">5</div>
          <div class="ab-spec-l">Steps in the<br>type scale</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ab-spec-n">15</div>
          <div class="ab-spec-l">Icons, one<br>shared grammar</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-ladder">

        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">01 — Foundations</p>
          <h3>Colour, type and icons, each with a rule attached.</h3>
          <p>
            Five colours, each with the share of a screen it should take: paper 50%, ink 28%,
            sage 15%, the two supporting sages 7%. A type scale of five named steps, from a
            108px display down to a 21px caption, each named for its job. Fifteen icons drawn
            on one grid with 2px strokes, no fills and rounded joins, plus a rule that any new
            icon joins the family before anyone reaches for a stock set.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">02 — Into the product</p>
          <h3>I applied it myself, and took the code review.</h3>
          <p>
            The interface, the icon set and the Smart Inbox navigation, written in CSS and
            JavaScript inside his repository and reviewed like anyone else's code. A few
            interface calls came out of that work: moving Run Audit inside the digest card,
            simplifying its toggle, and fixing how empty lists render.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">03 — Consistency</p>
          <h3>One system across every surface it touches.</h3>
          <p>
            The same foundations carried into the digest email, the marketing site and a
            launch booth, with printed table runners, die-cut stickers in four colourways and
            two looping reels.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="ab-media">
        <img src="/feeds/feeds-ui-smartinbox.webp" alt="The feeds Smart Inbox: twelve articles matching a saved firewall filter, each carrying rows of extracted CVE and IOC tags beneath its title." loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <p class="ab-caption">The Smart Inbox. Dense by nature, so the system does the quieting.</p>

      <div class="ab-media-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="ab-media">
            <img src="/feeds/guidelines-06.webp" alt="feeds guidelines, colour palette page: ink, sage, sage dark, sage light and paper with hex and RGB values, above a usage-ratio bar." loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="ab-caption">Colour, with the ratio each one gets.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ab-media">
            <img src="/feeds/guidelines-08.webp" alt="feeds guidelines, iconography page: fifteen custom icons sharing 2px strokes, no fill and rounded joins on one grid." loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="ab-caption">Fifteen icons, one grammar.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-media-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="ab-media">
            <img src="/feeds/guidelines-07.webp" alt="feeds guidelines, typography page: Bricolage Grotesque with a five-step type scale from Display to Caption." loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="ab-caption">A type scale named for what each step is for.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ab-media">
            <img src="/feeds/feeds-ui-articles.webp" alt="The feeds article list after the brand refresh, with inline CVE, malware and actor tags." loading="lazy" />
          </div>
          <p class="ab-caption">The article list, after the system went in.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-cta-links">
        <a href="/feeds.html" class="main-link">read the full case study &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="ab-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════ PROJECT 02 — ONWARD ═══════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="onward" class="ab-section">
      <p class="ab-section-label">Project 02 — A shipped AI product</p>
      <div class="ab-project-head">
        <h2 class="ab-project-title">Onward</h2>
        <span class="ab-meta">Product Designer &amp; Lead Developer · Sept – Dec 2024</span>
      </div>
      <p class="ab-lede">
        An AI interview coach for internationally educated healthcare professionals, mostly
        nurses, who are qualified for the jobs they apply to and need practice speaking up
        for themselves in interviews. Our team was all designers, and we split the startup
        roles between us. I took lead developer because I had the most build experience.
      </p>

      <div class="ab-tags">
        <span class="ab-tag">AI Product</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Speech-to-Text</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Prototype to Production</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Usability Testing</span>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-ladder">

        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">01 — My part</p>
          <h3>I turned the team's designs into the product.</h3>
          <p>
            I chose the stack, decided what was technically possible, and built the
            architecture and every screen. That meant live transcription with
            Azure Speech-to-Text, real-time filler-word detection, STAR-method scaffolding,
            a timer that counts up in practice and down in a mock, and a loading state on
            every async action.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">02 — The test</p>
          <h3>Twelve users, and a redesign before launch.</h3>
          <p>
            Ease of use came back at 8 out of 10, and what testers wanted changed was the
            feedback flow, so we redesigned it before we shipped.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="ab-stats">
        <div>
          <div class="ab-stat-n">8/10</div>
          <div class="ab-stat-l">Ease of use, 12 users</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ab-stat-n">4</div>
          <div class="ab-stat-l">Months to shipped</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="ab-stat-n">200+</div>
          <div class="ab-stat-l">Presented to, live</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-media">
        <img src="/ONWARD-main.webp" alt="The Onward dashboard, with practice and mock interview entry points, saved resumes and interview history." loading="lazy" />
      </div>

      <p class="ab-note">
        Onward was pitched to VANTEC Network angel investors and presented live to more than
        200 professionals, investors and government officials. The research and the product
        design decisions belonged to the team; the build was mine.
      </p>

      <div class="ab-cta-links">
        <a href="https://onward-p2.vercel.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="main-link">see it running &#8599;</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="ab-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════ PROJECT 03 — RAINBOWVI ═══════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="rainbowvi" class="ab-section">
      <p class="ab-section-label">Project 03 — Research through to web and mobile</p>
      <div class="ab-project-head">
        <h2 class="ab-project-title">RainbowVI</h2>
        <span class="ab-meta">UX/UI Designer (Internship) · Apr – May 2025</span>
      </div>
      <p class="ab-lede">
        A two-month placement that completed my BCIT diploma. I redesigned an educational
        association's MVP web app, starting from the people who would use it.
      </p>

      <div class="ab-tags">
        <span class="ab-tag">User Interviews</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Surveys</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Personas</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Journey Maps</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">Web &amp; Mobile</span>
        <span class="ab-tag">WCAG</span>
      </div>

      <div class="ab-ladder">
        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">01 — Research</p>
          <h3>Interviews, surveys and a look at the competition.</h3>
          <p>
            Those became the personas and journey maps the redesign was built on.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ab-step">
          <p class="ab-step-n">02 — Design</p>
          <h3>Interactive Figma prototypes, for web and mobile.</h3>
          <p>
            I designed screens for both web and mobile, and worked with the developers on
            responsive, WCAG-compliant interfaces.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- RAINBOWVI-MEDIA: screens go here once supplied -->
    </section>

    <div class="ab-divider"></div>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════ ABOUT / CTA ═══════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="about" class="ab-section" style="min-height: 90vh;">
      <p class="ab-section-label">About</p>
      <h2 class="ab-h2">Where I am,<br>plainly.</h2>
      <p class="ab-lede">
        I'm in Vancouver and would relocate to Mountain View for this role. As a Canadian I
        would work in the US on TN status, which I apply for with an offer letter, and I'm
        glad to handle that process.
      </p>
      <p class="ab-lede">
        I hold a Bachelor of Creative Industries and a Diploma in Digital Design &amp;
        Development, both from BCIT. Before that I studied cognitive science and digital
        humanities at the University of Toronto.
      </p>
      <p class="ab-lede">
        A data platform is only as good as the people who can use it at speed. That is the
        kind of interface I want to spend my days on.
      </p>

      <div class="ab-cta-links">
        <a href="mailto:hello@rawanaladdin.com" class="main-link">hello@rawanaladdin.com &#8599;</a>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rawan-aladdin" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="main-link">linkedin &#8599;</a>
        <a href="/projects.html" class="main-link">full portfolio &#8599;</a>
      </div>

      <p class="ab-footnote">
        Made for Abaka AI — October 2026.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>
</BaseLayout>
